<article class="env-variant" id="04JU">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04JU">Variant <span data-tag="04JU">6.3.6.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set and let $\psi _{S}: \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Sd}(S)$ be the comparison map of Construction <a data-tag="04HN" href="/tag/04HN">3.3.3.10</a>. Then $\psi _{S}$ is universally localizing. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that the functor $S \mapsto \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S} )$ preserves small colimits (Variant <a data-tag="04HQ" href="/tag/04HQ">3.3.3.20</a>). Proceeding as in the proof of Proposition <a data-tag="02ME" href="/tag/02ME">6.3.6.2</a>, we can reduce to the case where $S = \Delta ^{n}$ is a standard simplex. In this case, we can identify $\psi _{S}$ with (the nerve of) the functor 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S} \rightarrow \operatorname{Chain}[n] \quad \quad (\alpha : [m] \rightarrow [n] \mapsto \mathrm{im}(\alpha ) \subseteq [n] ) \]
</div>
<p>
       This functor admits a section $\phi $, which identifies $\operatorname{Chain}[n]$ with the subcategory $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S}^{\mathrm{nd}} \subseteq \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S}$ of <em>nondegenerate</em> simplices of $S$. Note that there is a (unique) natural transformation from the identity functor $\operatorname{id}_{ \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S} }$ to $\phi \circ \psi _{S}$ which belongs to $\operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{Sd}(S) }( \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S} ), \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{S} ) )$, so the desired result follows from the criterion of Proposition <a data-tag="04JT" href="/tag/04JT">6.3.5.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
